  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220C={30}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220C,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220C) & =\\frac{AB}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({30}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-1)}{2x+1} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(2x+1) & =3\\sqrt{3}(x-1) \\\\ 2x+1 & =3x-3 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{3}(x-1)=\\sqrt{3}(4-1)=3\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ BC & =2x+1=2(4)+1=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =\\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
